{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "framework": "playwright",
  "testId": "testim-migrated/tests/webstore/shopping-cart/verify-multicoupon-not-allowed-when-flag-disabled.spec.ts > Webstore - Shopping Cart > verify multicoupon not allowed when flag disabled",
  "scenario": {
    "summary": "A registered user applies a Percent Off Product coupon to two products raised to quantity 5, then tries an Amount Off Order coupon that does not allow clubbing: it is rejected with the clubbing message and the discount stays at the first coupon's percent. No order.",
    "steps": [
      "Sign in as the registered user, empty the cart and remove all coupons",
      "Add sku1 and sku2 at qty 1; SKU labels show sku1 and sku2 (lines found by name1, name2)",
      "Apply couponCode1, raise both lines to updatedQuantity: success message and code at index 0",
      "Apply couponCode2: invalid message at index 1 is the clubbing errorMessage, invalid code at index 1 is couponCode2, label 0 still couponCode1",
      "Discount unchanged and equal to discountAmount% x subtotal",
      "Remove all coupons, empty cart, log out"
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "product",
      "promotion",
      "user",
      "cart"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [
      "Both coupons are created per run through the API (consumable COUPON_* keys); the test only applies and removes them, no order is placed",
      "Registered user's cart: products added, coupons applied/removed, emptied at cleanup"
    ],
    "assertions": [
      "SKU labels equal \"SKU: \" + sku1 / sku2",
      "Coupon message at index 0 equals \"- \" + promoAppliedSuccesssMessage; label 0 equals couponCode1",
      "Invalid message at index 1 equals \"- \" + errorMessage; invalid code at index 1 equals couponCode2; label 0 still couponCode1",
      "Discount after equals discount before (precision 2) and is close to subtotal x discountAmount/100",
      "Empty cart message visible; sign-in link visible after logout"
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "Title: 'verify multicoupon not allowed when flag disabled'",
      "User decision: no store key; the 'flag' is each coupon's Is Allowed With Other Coupon - coupon1 as in the allowed spec (true), coupon2 an Amount Off Order coupon with allowedWithOtherCoupons false",
      "Note: the old second coupon RETAILCPN15 (Amount Off Order, 15.0) has orderMinimum $500, which the cart (two products at qty 5) may not have met - the rejection may have come from the minimum, not from clubbing. The created coupon2 has order minimum 0 (COUPON_AMOUNT_OFF_ORDER collection constant), so the cart meets it and only the clubbing rule can reject it",
      "coupon2 discountAmount 15.0 comes from the profiled RETAILCPN15; the test does not assert it",
      "Profile: PRODUCT10 (Percent Off Product, 10.0, orderMinimum 400) on MaxwellsHardware; sku1 z-2100007 and sku2 z-2100005 are active in-stock simple products",
      "No profile check: both coupons apply to every profile (allProfiles true)",
      "Discount assertions use the resolved coupon1 discountAmount (role data), not the literal 10.00",
      "coupon2 orderMinimum left out: the collection default (0) is met by any cart",
      "Links: coupon1 is created for both products (productId @product1.productId, secondProductId @product2.productId), so the discount is asserted over both lines as the original spec does (User decision)",
      "User decision 2026-10-29 (C2b): notDiscountedForProfile Retail Customer on both products: the whole test runs signed in",
      "User decision 2026-10-29 (C2d): signed-in cart (Retail order minimum 650): product1 + product2 at qty 5 each -> 5 x (p1 + p2) < 650 -> each price < 65 -> maxPrice 65"
    ],
    "confidence": "medium",
    "needsReview": true
  },
